From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: the process snapshot API (PssCaptureSnapshot and the rest)

kernel32 did not export PssCaptureSnapshot, PssQuerySnapshot, PssFreeSnapshot
and the rest. A loader that resolves a DLL's imports itself stops at the first
missing one: BleachBit's UPX-packed python312.dll looks up PssQuerySnapshot
(CPython's os.getppid uses it), its DllMain failed, and BleachBit died in a
stack overflow. A snapshot holds the process's information (its ids, parent,
times, memory counters, image name); clones, handles, threads and the address
space are not captured (ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED when asked for), and a walk ends
at once. Written from the documented API; processsnapshot.h is new.
---
--- a/include/Makefile.in
+++ b/include/Makefile.in
@@ -637,6 +637,7 @@
 	poppack.h \
 	powrprof.h \
 	prntvpt.h \
+	processsnapshot.h \
 	processthreadsapi.h \
 	profinfo.h \
 	proofofpossessioncookieinfo.idl \
